sec.p:
A supercapacitor was tested in a symmetrical two electrode cell configuration. A test fixture consists of two stainless steel plates and the two electrode assembly is made of two current collectors (carbon-coated Al foil), two carbon electrodes, and a porous separator (Celgard 3501). The electrode was prepared by mixing a-BGC with poly(tetrafluoroethylene) (PTFE, 60 wt% water dispersion, Sigma Aldrich) at a a-BGC:PTFE weight ratio of 95:5. The mixture was rolled to thicknesses of ~ 35 and 180 μm, punched (10 mm diameter), and was dried in an oven at 100 °C for 24 h. The mass of the electrode was 0.7 mg and the apparent density of the electrode was 0.25 g cm−3. 1-ethyl-3-methylimidazolium bis(trifluoromethylsulfonyl)imide (EMIM-TFSI) diluted in acetonitrile (AN) with a weight ratio of 1:1 was used as an electrolyte. Cyclic voltammetry (CV), galvanostatic charge-discharge and electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) were examined using Potentiostat (Autolab). The specific capacitance, Csp (F g−1) was calculated from the galvanostatic charge-discharge curves according to the equation (1).1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
